{
 "_comment": [
  "The DSP effect data tables: how an effect's VALUE byte becomes a physical",
  "quantity. Transcribed from Technics' Reference Guide page 33, which is",
  "image-only and was rendered and read.",
  "",
  "Every arithmetic row carries first value, last value and step, and",
  "sysex_conversion_tables.py asserts v_lo + step*(p_hi - p_lo) == v_hi for each",
  "one. A misread endpoint or step breaks that identity, so the transcription",
  "checks itself row by row.",
  "",
  "'packings' are the guide's tables 17 and 18 and its pre/post equaliser note:",
  "three fields sharing two bytes. Each field's width must be wide enough for",
  "the range of the table it carries, which the probe also asserts."
 ],
